e where the market  Criers we have here and a fresh fish  bidding Donson fish fish  five o'clock the market is open for  business  on a good day some 70,000 visitors come  here a cafe next to the market  seed everyone is enjoying a bit of calm  before the storm soon he'll take his  place  at center stage  smoke deland wild salmon artists  specialties as soon as the stand opens  the shoppers are waiting and looking  forward to being entertained moon is one  of the most colorful characters at the  market and an institution in his own  right  sales patter is all part of the  experience  didja trained as a mechanical engineer  but found his true calling as a  fishmonger he used to sell fish at  markets during the week - I love  interacting with people at helping  people man they enjoy the chance to  laugh they enjoy my jokes  Thank You Mimi that's  at 7:00 a.m. the crowds have arrived  some early arrivals are heading home  from a night on the town locals tourists  even the fishmongers they all love this  Sunday morning market  we thought we'd round things off with a  visit to the fish market we often come  here when we've been out partying we  just go and grab a fish roll and Samael  it's a bit like a show we've got  relatives staying right now this is my  sister this is a professor from Ukraine  we're here so they can see the show the  are tuna fish market has been a local  landmark since 17:03 back then the fish  was supposed to be sold before everyone  went to church and sleep early start  today visitors can also buy souvenirs  flowers fruit and sweet treats the fish  vendors love entertaining their visitors  they're famous for their banter and for  their loud voices it's more relaxed here  than the usual weekday markets everyone  hears on first-name terms in a good mood  it's a traditional market and it's good  fun we get all the night owls we get  tourists we all joke around it's a good  laugh at eight o'clock it's already  pouring rain as is often the case in  Ham